  "result": "Excellent! All 135 tests pass. Here's what I've implemented:\n\n**src/dates.js** \u2014 Date utilities in UTC:\n\n**`isValidDate(text)`** \u2014 Validates YYYY-MM-DD format:\n- Checks format with regex\n- Verifies it's a real date (rejects Feb 30, etc.)\n- Handles leap years correctly\n- Works only with UTC times\n\n**`addDays(date, n)`** \u2014 Adds n days to a date (UTC):\n- Positive n adds days forward\n- Negative n subtracts days backward\n- Handles month/year boundaries\n- Returns YYYY-MM-DD string\n\n**`daysBetween(a, b)`** \u2014 Calculates whole days (b - a):\n- Returns integer number of days\n- Positive when b is later than a\n- Negative when b is earlier than a\n- Works across month/year boundaries\n- Uses UTC arithmetic\n\n**src/invoices.js** \u2014 Updated:\n- Imports `isValidDate` from dates.js\n- Removed local date validation function\n- Uses centralized date validation\n\n**Design decision:** All dates are YYYY-MM-DD strings. All arithmetic uses UTC (via `T00:00:00Z` suffix) to avoid timezone-related bugs. No local time conversions.\n\n**Tests** \u2014 22 comprehensive tests covering:\n- Format validation (valid/invalid, edge cases)\n- Real date validation (Feb 29 on leap/non-leap years)\n- Day addition (positive, negative, zero, boundaries)\n- Day differences (same date, forward, backward)\n- Leap years (2024, 2000, 2100)\n- Consistency between addDays and daysBetween\n- Large numbers (365+ days)\n\nAll 135 tests pass \u2713",
